_pdbx_entry_details.entry_id                   1QLL 
_pdbx_entry_details.compound_details           
;THE PHOSPHOLIPASES A2 (PLA2) CAN BE DIVIDED INTO TWO MAJOR
 CLASSES BASED UPON CATALYTIC ACTIVITY. THE D49 CLASS IS
 ACTIVE, WHILE THE K49 CLASS IS INACTIVE. THE SEQUENCE
 NUMBERING IS BASED ON A REPRESENTATIVE PHOSPHOLIPASE A2.
 IN THE K49 PLA2 CLASS ENZYME STUDIED HERE THE LYS IS
 RESIDUE 48. SIGNIFICANTLY THIS K49 ENZYME, DESPITE ITS LACK
 OF PHOSPHOLIPASE ACTION, SHOWS SEVERAL PHARMACOLOGICAL
 EFFECTS.
 THE STRUCTURE REVEALS THE PRESENCE OF A FATTY ACID MOLECULE
 TRAPPED IN THE REACTION SITE OF EACH ENZYME MOLECULE.
;
